# CODEOWNERS -- who must approve a change to an approval ledger (B448, ADR-209 items 2 and 3).
#
# A "ledger" is a pinned file in which a ratchet check records what the human approved: a
# weakening marker, a tolerance, a parameter id, a build flag, a licence exception, a golden
# self-digest, an accepted limit or a hole expiry. If an agent can edit a ledger and merge, it
# can approve its own change. This file names the human as the owner of every ledger, so a pull
# request that touches one needs the human's review.
#
# THIS FILE BINDS NOTHING BY ITSELF. GitHub enforces it only while the main branch ruleset has
# "Require review from Code Owners" switched on, and only for a pull request whose author is
# not the owner. That toggle is the human's, and is switched on only once agent pull requests
# come from the separate machine account (a pull request from the human's own account cannot
# be approved by the human). Until then this file is a record, and
# tools/ledger_owner_check.py guards it.
#
# ONLY LEDGERS GET AN OWNER. There is deliberately no catch-all `*` rule. To add a ledger: add
# its rule here AND its path in tools/ledger_owner_check.py (LEDGERS); that check is red if the
# two disagree, or if a ratchet tool pins a file that is in neither.

